venu-pacific (26.08) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release. Everything Venu Pacific-specific moves out of
    live-build's includes.chroot and into real Debian packages, so an
    installed system can receive updates through "apt update" instead of
    only through a new 4.7GB image.
  * New venu-pacific-archive-keyring: ships the archive signing key and the
    apt source entry pointing at https://download.venupacific.org/apt.
  * The release version is now defined once, here. /etc/venu-pacific-release,
    the os-release fields, the Help page and the installer title all derive
    from it, replacing the two live-build hooks that used to set it (and
    disagreed with each other about PRETTY_NAME).

